Subject: Read execd image artifacts without starting a runtime
Base-Commit: 97031ea81fee1b853e4cd89e5490b1be9f5ead55
Upstream: https://github.com/opensandbox-group/OpenSandbox
License: Apache-2.0

The standard archive API can read image files from a created container.
Do not start a helper merely to extract those files: alternative OCI runtimes
can make their running rootfs unavailable to the engine archive implementation.
Keep workload runtime selection unchanged. Test cache reuse and cleanup after
both successful reads and archive errors, without inspecting the engine vendor.

